==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 3~14 seconds<sup>90f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 3~14 seconds<sup>90f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 6~14 seconds<sup>180f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 6~14 seconds<sup>180f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 66.67~100 seconds<sup>2,000f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 66.67~100 seconds<sup>2,000f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Le'boin]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
At this point, you should have 300% Empire of Cats treasures for this level. Otherwise, it will be far more tricky than it needs to be.

It is strongly suggested to start off the attack by deploying meatshields to stall the Zoges and Znaches, as well as instantly deal with their burrows, then proceed to upgrade your Worker Cat to level 3. Once you reach that level, save up for a Mythical Titan to clear out the peons.

The main difficulty arises once the Zories and Zir Zeals begin to spawn. Continue sending out your meatshields and proceed to spawn longer ranged units such as Sexy Legs Cats, Dragon Cats, Paris Cats, True Valkyrie Cat or Crazed Bahamut Cat, as they will help out against the Le'Boins, as Crazed Bahamut Cat can outrange and chip away at the Le'Boin before another one can spawn in. If you have any Rare Anti-Zombie units, such as Gardener Cat, they will help out a ton against the Zombie units.

You should be able to win if you are frequent with your meatshield deployment, and can deal with the Zombies' Burrow and Revives.

